  "notes": "A bootleg/mash-up producer turned synth-pop hitmaker — \"synthesised, grungy pop music\": 92–128 straight, backbeat on 2&4. The harmony is stated as a bass fact: \"two-chord ostinatos where the **bass riff is the harmony**\", with \"minor-tonic vamps with a flattened-7th colour\", so `maxChords` is 2, the harmonic rhythm leans on `vamp`, the mixolydian/dorian flat-7 colour is in the scales, and the bassline runs `independent_riff` at 0.3 — the freest bass in this section — with authored cell shapes because \"the bass playing a repeating riff rather than roots… **is the hook**\". Three drum deltas are quoted: \"hard gated snare on 2&4\" (a loud accent with the clap offset at zero), \"kick on 1 and 3&\", and \"808-style cowbell/tom accents\" plus stacked handclaps, which is the cowbell/tom/snap perc block; the kit is \"intentionally rough and spiky\", which is why the hats are heavily filtered — a mix property the model expresses as a low hat velocity band. The architecture is the mash-up itself: \"a cold, mechanical synth bed with a deadpan human vocal on top; the instrumental hook answers each vocal phrase\", so the melody sits low and flat and the counter is a high-ratio answer lick. ⚠ `confidence` is medium because the research rates it high-medium and says the tempo band is catalogue-derived. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are every drum probability, the bass cell shapes and `bpm.mode` 112.",
